        <description>PERFORM EO.23/084 (B) COMPONENT (ENGINEERING ORDER) REV. 00
PARTNO : CFMLEAP-1B / SERIALNO : 60A102
         ENGINE CFM LEAP-1B
         POS: #1

LEAP -  FUEL NOZZLE - FULL SET REPLACEMENT


LEAP -  FUEL NOZZLE - FULL SET REPLACEMENT


BACKGROUND: LEAP 1B NOZZLES FULL SET REPLACEMENT IN ORDER TO MINIMISE OPERATIONAL DISRUPTION DUE TO HEAT SHIELD DISTRESS AND FUEL NOZZLE COKING CNRS.  LEAP SB 73-0042 REQUIRES NOZZLES ARE REMOVED PRIOR TO 4550FC  

NOTE THIS IS A CRITICAL TASK.
ACTION:
1.OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS GAIN ACCESS TO THE APPLICABLE ENG.

2.REMOVE THE COMPLTE FUEL NOZZLE SET IAW AMM TASK
73-11-05-000-802-G00:

A: SOAK ALL APPLICABLE BOLTS IN CP2691 PENETRATING FLUID FOR A
MINIMUM OF 1 HOUR PRIOR TO BREAKING TORQUE.

B: MAKE SURE THAT YOU COVER ALL PORTS, OPENINGS, MATING SURFACES, AND
CASES. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY, FOD CAN GO INTO THE COMPONENTS AND DAMAGE
CAN OCCUR.

C: WHEN REMOVING THE FOUR FUEL NOZZLE BOLTS DO NOT REMOVE THE BOLTS
TOO QUICKLY. THE BOLTS CAN BECOME HOT AND SEIZE. IF YOU DO NOT OBEY,
DAMAGE TO BOLTS AND THREADS CAN OCCUR.

3. INSTALL A NEW FUEL NOZZLE SET IAW AMM TASK 73-11-05-400-802-G00
.ENSURE THE FOLLOWING IS CARRIED OUT DURING THE INSTALLATION:

A: ENSURE THE NEW FUEL NOZZLE BOLTS ARE PREPARED WITH D50355.

B: C/O A VISUAL INSPECTION OF THE NEW FUEL NOZZLE, THE NEW FUEL
NOZZLE SEAL AND THE MATING SURFACES FOR ANY SIGN OF DAMAGE.

 C: ENSURE THE ATTACHED FUEL NOZZLE TORQUE CHECK DOCUMENT IS
COMPLETED FOR FUEL  NOZZLE SET AND RETURNED TO
POWERPLANT@RYANAIR.COM.

NOTE:  PAY PARTICULAR ATTENTION TO FUEL NOZZLE GASKET CORRECT INSTALLATION FOR NOZZLES POSTION 17,18,1,2 &amp;3 WHERE ACCESS IS LIMITED. 

NOTE: ENSURE THE HPSOV IS ALIGNED CORRECTLY IAW AMM  TASK 36-11-07-400-801 FIGURE 401 SHEET 2 AND TT 36-002.

NOTE: ENSURE THE FUEL LINES TO THE SBV ARE TORQUED CORRECTLY PER AMM REQUIREMENTS. 

 4 . FOLLOWING INSTALLATION OF THE FUEL NOZZLE ENSURE THE FOLLOWING
ARE ACOMPLISHED:

A:  TEST AS REQUIRED BY AMM TASK 71-00-00-800-804-G00 FOR FUEL NOZZLE
REPLACEMENT:

-IDLE LEAK CHECK IAW TASK 71-00-00-790-804-G00 . SEE FOOTNOTE 7
REGARDING EEC FAULTS DUE TO RESIDUAL AIR IN THE FUEL LINES FOLLOWING
FUEL NOZZLE REPLACEMENT.

B:  IF YOU OPEN THE EEC AIR SIGNAL MANIFOLDS WHEN YOU REMOVE AND
INSTALL THE FUEL NOZZLE C/O THE APPLICABLE TEST FOR AIR DUCTS AND AIR
TUBES IAW AMM TASK 71-00-00-800-804-G00:

NOTE: PAY PARTICULAR ATTENTION TO THE 4TH &amp; 7TH STAGE BLEED AIR
DUCTS.

-DO A VISUAL CHECK ON ALL NON LRU AIR TUBES OR DUCTS THAT WERE
DISCONNECTED OR REMOVED FOR ENGINE MAINTENANCE.
-PNEUMATIC LEAK CHECK IAW AMM TASK 71-00-00-790-801-G00

5. C/O TEST NO.6 POWER ASSURANCE TEST IAW AMM TASK
71-00-00-720-802-G00.

6. RETURN THE ENG TO A SERVICEABLE CONDITION.</description>
